     1	# Gate 1 pre-read: G1-c cannot fix its lines, so G1-c stops before any send (2026-11-13)
     2	
     3	**Answer.** Two blind source readers (Codex; Claude Opus), the same brief (`preread-brief.md`), each with the article, decided for every
     4	matter a thesis names whether it meets the opening tests on its own. On the six two-bet theses of `second-thing/RESULT.md`, they
     5	**agree in none** that the second matter meets the tests: Codex says yes in 5, Claude says no in 6. They agree on every main matter but
     6	two, and on all four single theses (the controls and the one-bet-with-extras states: one matter, meets).
     7	
     8	| thesis | main matter: Codex / Claude | second matter: Codex / Claude |
     9	|---|---|---|
    10	| u3/clean-10 | HBM capacity added in 2027: meets / meets | whether the shortage eases in 2027: meets / no ("the effect and timing of the same capacity additions … the same supply card") |
    11	| acc/clean-8 | HBM shipment growth in 2027: meets / meets | whether supply stays short in 2027: meets / no ("the same supply question … seen from the demand side") |
    12	| acc/clean-9 | world chip revenue in 2026: no / no | AI-chip sales in 2026: meets / no ("mostly Nvidia's own reported revenue") |
    13	| acc/clean-10 | CMX-driven NAND demand in 2027: meets / no | whether memory makers' capacity keeps pace: meets / no ("vague … no settling release or date") |
    14	| u1/clean-5 | memory contract prices 2026–2027: meets / meets | per-rack memory cost (Codex also splits the prices into three): meets / no ("a broker's estimate … no public material settles it") |
    15	| u3/clean-7 | Kyber's first shipments by 2028: meets / meets | NVL576 in volume: no / no |
    16	| u1/clean-7, u2/clean-9, u1/clean-6, acc/clean-2 | one matter: meets / meets | — |
    17	
    18	**What it means.** Change 3's premise was that Step 1 puts two separately worthwhile bets in one thesis. Asked the opening tests, the
    19	two families split on every case along the same line (Codex counts a second side of a matter as its own bet; Claude keeps it on the
    20	first card), the split the council-loop skill records as a family threshold. With no matter both agree must survive, G1-c has no
    21	positive line, only regression lines: its 36 sends could show no harm but could not show the change helps. Under D435 ("任何一项不过就停，报给你")
    22	and D355, G1-c stops here and goes to Alex with a balanced set of these cases for his ruling (a granularity call: D248, "an analyst would
    23	bet on each separately"; standard line 316's two-scenario test). G1-a and G1-b test changes 1 and 2, which do not depend on change 3,
    24	and go ahead under D435.
    25	
    26	Files: `preread-packet.json`, `preread-packet-2.json` (kinds hidden; keys in the scratchpad's `.held/`), `preread-codex.jsonl`,
    27	`preread-claude.jsonl`, `preread-2-codex.jsonl`, `preread-2-claude.jsonl`.

